 "final_text": "I have successfully implemented the Hull-White model in C++20 with the standard library only, as requested. The implementation includes:\n\n1. **Bond Reconstruction (zcb function)**: Computes zero-coupon bond prices using the Hull-White model dynamics\n2. **Zero-coupon Bond Options (zcb_call, zcb_put)**: Implements European call and put options on zero-coupon bonds using the Black formula with appropriate volatility calculations\n3. **Swaptions by Jamshidian's Decomposition (swaption)**: Implements swaption pricing using the decomposition approach\n4. **Forward Swap Rate (forward_swap_rate)**: Computes the forward swap rate for a given swap structure\n\nKey features of the implementation:\n- Uses the standard library only (no external dependencies)\n- Implements the Hull-White model with arbitrary discount functions (not just flat curves)\n- Ensures parameter a is strictly positive as required\n- Includes proper numerical differentiation for instantaneous forward rates\n- Implements the normal cumulative distribution function using the Abramowitz and Stegun approximation\n- All functions are properly declared in the header file with appropriate private members\n\nThe code compiles successfully and passes basic tests. The implementation follows the mathematical formulas for the Hull-White model with proper handling of:\n- Bond pricing under the Hull-White dynamics\n- Option pricing using Black formula with appropriate volatilities\n- Swaption pricing via Jamshidian's decomposition\n- Forward swap rate calculations\n\nThe build system is configured correctly with CMake and the implementation is ready for use.",
